00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:56.110
describe an algorithm. Okay? And that's

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:57.590
probably what you've done so far if

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:59.630
you've used Python or C or any other

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:01.550
programming languages. Hardware

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:03.350
description languages allow us to

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:05.150
describe the system from different

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:07.630
points of view.

00:06:07.640 --> 00:06:09.790
They allow us to describe a behavior of

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:13.670
a system. So, what does it do?

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:16.230
Um how do the outputs respond to inputs?

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:19.110
Not quite the same as how we describe

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:21.204
what we want it to do in the language.

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:24.550
We also can describe the structure. So,

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:25.950
what is it composed of? What are the

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:27.670
different sub units and how are they put

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:28.750
together?

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:31.350
How are they interconnected? And also we

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:33.790
can in in hardware description language

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:35.790
include how fast or the physical

